*HELPMODE
You may select what portions of the software to install or update.

The prime reason for installing only part of the software is to save
Hard Disk space. If disk space is not an issue we recommend you
install ALL of the software.
*HELPCOMMAND
The COMMAND.COM is used by the menu to generate DOS shell environments.

It is necessary to have this file on the directory PATH that is normally
set-up in the AUTOEXEC.BAT at system boot-up. The install procedure will
include the path set here at installation on the DOS PATH statement.
*HELPROOT
The installation process will create the following directory structure:
                  ... --><PALASM root>
				|--> EXE
				|--> DAT
                                |--> LIB
                                |--> DOC
                                |-->  |-->EREF
                                |-->  |-->IREF
                                |-->  |-->LREF
                                |--> EXAMPLES
                                |-->  |-->CB
                                |-->  |-->WB
PALASM has it own Directory structure from the root directory specified
at installation.
*HELPDRIVE
PALASM can be installed on any logical drive existing on your Hard Disk.
*HELPAUTOEXEC
Enter 'Y' if we can automatically update your AUTOEXEC.BAT file to include
the necessary statements to make PALASM operational.

Enter 'N' and these statements will be written to a file. You must include
these statements yourself be PALASM will be operational.
*HELPAUTOFILE
Name of file to use if you have entered 'N' to the previous entry.
*HELPCONFIG
Enter 'Y' if we can automatically update your CONFIG.SYS file to include
the necessary statements to make PALASM operational.

Enter 'N' and these statements will be written to a file. You must include
these statements yourself be PALASM will be operational.
*HELPCONFILE
Name of file to use if you have entered 'N' to the previous entry.
*HELPORCADDRIVE
ORCAD can be installed on any logical drive existing on your Hard Disk.
*HELPORCADINT
If you intend to use PALASM with the ORCAD SDT editor you must install
the PALASM interface to ORCAD. Enter 'Y' to install else the relevant
PALASM executables & libraries will not be installed on your hard disk.

You may install the ORCAD interface only at a later date by selecting
the correct install option & entering 'Y' here.
*HELPMOUSE
PALASM allows installation of a mouse to work with your PC software.

note:
        2 Button mice must be compatible with the Microsoft Mouse.

        3 Button mice must be compatible with either Logitech or
          PC Mouse Systems mice.
*HELPEDITOR
PALASM provides a comprehensive Text Editor for your use, check manual for
instructions. If you prefer then you may use your personal editor by
entering  the path and program name.

WARNING!!! 
   If you use your own editor it must operate in TEXT mode and not use the
   special documentation modes for output formating .
